## Shared Web planning refinement ΓÇö exact broker account targeting and staged credential replacement

Owner clarified the credential-recovery UX for users who may have multiple accounts/APIs at the same broker.

Shared Web planning now requires:

- exact broker + broker account identifier + environment to be presented to the user before any reset/rotation guidance;
- broker name alone is insufficient when one user has multiple accounts or API credentials at the same broker;
- the newly entered credential is staged as `PENDING_VALIDATION`, not treated as active on submit;
- the previously stored Falcon credential is retained temporarily and is not deleted merely because the user entered a replacement;
- the Application validates the candidate against the intended account/environment and returns the authoritative validation result;
- only after successful validation/promotion is the old stored credential eligible for secure removal;
- if the broker reset itself invalidates the old key externally, Falcon local retention must not be presented as proof that the old credential remains usable;
- incident resolution still depends on the Application's authoritative recovery/reconciliation semantics, not credential entry alone.

