## Shared Web planning update ΓÇö Owner follow-up after no-reply alert dismiss

Owner decision recorded in Shared Web planning:

- the five-minute viewed/no-reply High Alert may be dismissed by the Owner;
- after Owner dismissal, the same no-reply alert SHALL NOT automatically reappear merely because the same user silence continues;
- dismissal means the Owner has taken ownership of the human follow-up signal, not that the user replied or the incident resolved;
- the Owner may contact the customer through normal external contact channels only, never by joining the user's Falcon Incident Conversation;
- if contact succeeds, the Owner may report the relevant contact result back to Falcon;
- if contact fails, the Owner may report that the customer could not be reached and the number of contact attempts;
- that contact-attempt/result information is an attributable human follow-up record only and does not become broker truth, trading authority, or incident-resolution authority.

